+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates tool call arguments against each tool's declared JSON Schema (`inputSchema`) before invoking its executor. Invalid inputs return a descriptive `ToolResponse` to the model so it can self-correct within the tool-loop round budget rather than throwing out of the turn, while unknown tool names continue to throw.
+
+## Schema Compilation and Caching
+
+- `ToolRegistry.register` compiles a static tool definition's `inputSchema` once at registration time, throwing an error that names the tool when the schema cannot be compiled, and reuses that compiled validator across calls ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool for an uncompilable schema, and compiles a static schema once across ten execute calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L117)).
+- For a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource`, `ToolRegistry.execute` resolves the current definition per call and validates against the schema current for that call rather than a stale cached validator ([validated by: validates a function-valued tool definition against the schema current at each call without using a stale cached schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L160)).
+- When a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` returns the same `inputSchema` object reference across calls, its compiled validator is cached by that schema object rather than recompiled on every call.
+
+## Input Validation and Error Reporting
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` enforces `required`, declared JSON Schema types, and `enum` without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types, or applying defaults, returning a `ToolResponse` naming missing required fields without invoking the executor while passing valid inputs with extra properties through unchanged ([validated by: returns a ToolResponse naming missing required fields without calling the executor, while passing valid input with extra properties unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L19)).
+- Rejection messages and log lines name the failing property paths and failed constraints (`type`, `enum`, `required`) and never include offending or identifying property values ([validated by: rejects wrong-typed fields and invalid enum values with path and constraint, omitting offending and identifying values from result and logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L57)).
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` when asked to execute an unregistered tool name.
+
+## Orchestrator Tool-Loop Integration
+
+- When `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a schema validation rejection, `ChatOrchestrator` forwards that rejection text in the round's `tool_result` message so the provider can retry with corrected input and resolve `processMessage` without throwing ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result so the provider can retry and resolve the message](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L19)).
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Returning an unknown tool name to the model instead of throwing `Unknown tool: <name>` remains tracked separately.
+- Validating tool output, hallucination detection, per-tool authorization, and retry/timeout/rate-limiting around tool execution are out of scope.
